I see a straight line with a ray originating from a point on it, forming two adjacent angles labeled $3x^\circ$ and $x^\circ$. Since they are adjacent and form a straight line, they must be supplementary — their sum is $180^\circ$. So I set up the equation $3x + x = 180$, which simplifies to $4x = 180$, then $x = 45$.

I should double-check: 3x = 135, x = 45, 135 + 45 = 180. Perfect. That’s consistent.

